    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0346" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/81: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-08T12:00:00+01:00">June 8,
                            1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 8—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>308. The Japanese Ambassador confirmed to me this morning that although he will
                    be prepared to discuss those subjects outlined by him <pb facs="0347" n="247"
                        xml:id="pg247"/> and reported in my 292, May 31, 5 p.m., he would not be
                    prepared to begin technical conversations until the Japanese naval experts had
                    reached London, sometime about the middle of July.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Davis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
